{"seed_cos": 0.671, "community_id": 22, "title": "Pregnancy exposures (influenza, interpregnancy interval, residence moves) and adverse birth outcomes", "summary": "These three papers study maternal exposures during pregnancy, namely influenza A(H1N1)pdm09 infection, short interpregnancy interval after a stillbirth, and residential change in the first trimester, and their links to adverse birth outcomes. The influenza paper reports an association with adverse birth outcomes (C1), and the residence-change paper says moving in the first trimester may be a risk factor (C3). The interpregnancy interval paper found no association with adverse outcomes (C2), a null result that differs from the two positive findings but does not contradict them because it concerns a different exposure. None of the three claims has a matched press statement, so press coverage cannot be compared with the papers.", "key_findings": [{"text": "Influenza A(H1N1)pdm09 infection during pregnancy is associated with adverse birth outcomes.", "claim_ids": ["e65a0c5545a9acea"]}, {"text": "Residential mobility during the first trimester of pregnancy may increase the risk of adverse birth outcomes.", "claim_ids": ["c2ad4e2c8317fd51"]}, {"text": "No association found between a short interpregnancy interval after a stillbirth and adverse birth outcomes.", "claim_ids": ["bc83152c3207d555"]}], "n_claims": 3, "n_papers": 3, "press_labels": {}, "key_claims": [{"claim_id": "e65a0c5545a9acea", "doi": "10.1002/bdr2.1445"}, {"claim_id": "bc83152c3207d555", "doi": "10.1016/s0140-6736(18)32266-9"}, {"claim_id": "c2ad4e2c8317fd51", "doi": "10.1136/jech-2018-211937"}]}
