{"seed_cos": 0.467, "community_id": 21, "title": "Maternal influenza ICU stays and moving linked to low birth weight", "summary": "These findings cover maternal exposures during pregnancy, namely ICU admission for 2009 H1N1 influenza and residential moves in the first trimester, and their link to birth outcomes, mainly low birth weight. Both claims report a positive association at strength 1 ('associated with'), so the papers do not conflict. The second paper's wording also mentions preterm birth as associated with first-trimester moves. Press releases matched both claims as aligned, so neither was overstated or understated relative to the paper. No retracted papers appear in this community.", "key_findings": [{"text": "Maternal ICU admission for 2009 H1N1 influenza is associated with low birth weight.", "claim_ids": ["b81f47a6e273d93d"]}, {"text": "Residential moves during the first trimester of pregnancy are associated with low birth weight.", "claim_ids": ["ff6a19e2677c9288"]}, {"text": "Press coverage of both papers' low birth weight findings was aligned with the strength of the papers' wording.", "claim_ids": ["b81f47a6e273d93d", "ff6a19e2677c9288"]}], "n_claims": 2, "n_papers": 2, "press_labels": {"aligned": 2}, "key_claims": [{"claim_id": "b81f47a6e273d93d", "doi": "10.1002/bdr2.1445"}, {"claim_id": "ff6a19e2677c9288", "doi": "10.1136/jech-2018-211937"}]}
