{"seed_cos": 0.283, "community_id": 33, "title": "Desulfovibrio bacteria and TFE3 effects on alpha-synuclein aggregation in Parkinson's models", "summary": "This community covers two studies of alpha-synuclein aggregation in Parkinson's disease models: one on Desulfovibrio bacteria in C. elegans and one on TFE3 in an AAV-alpha-synuclein model. The two papers conflict in direction, since the Desulfovibrio study reports an increase in aggregation (associated with, strength 1) while the TFE3 study reports a decrease (reduces, strength 3). The Desulfovibrio paper also includes a conditional statement that Desulfovibrio may contribute to PD development by inducing aggregation (strength 2). Press coverage of the Desulfovibrio association was overstated in one release and aligned in another, while the TFE3 finding was understated and the conditional Desulfovibrio claim had no press match. No papers in this community are retracted.", "key_findings": [{"text": "Worms fed Desulfovibrio bacteria from PD patients were associated with more and larger alpha-synuclein aggregates than worms fed healthy-donor Desulfovibrio or E. coli.", "claim_ids": ["7d43c4cdbd1a82d5"]}, {"text": "TFE3 overexpression reduces alpha-synuclein aggregation.", "claim_ids": ["3234385932fcc938"]}, {"text": "Desulfovibrio bacteria may contribute to PD development by inducing alpha-syn aggregation.", "claim_ids": ["9434c54a3813a8d4"]}, {"text": "Press coverage overstated the Desulfovibrio association in one release and understated the TFE3 finding.", "claim_ids": ["7d43c4cdbd1a82d5", "3234385932fcc938"]}], "n_claims": 3, "n_papers": 2, "press_labels": {"understated": 1, "overstated": 1, "aligned": 1}, "key_claims": [{"claim_id": "3234385932fcc938", "doi": "10.1016/j.gendis.2024.101429"}, {"claim_id": "7d43c4cdbd1a82d5", "doi": "10.3389/fcimb.2023.1181315"}, {"claim_id": "9434c54a3813a8d4", "doi": "10.3389/fcimb.2023.1181315"}]}

